;	sys/kern/syscalls.master - the native system calls of V86BSD.
;
;	number	type	{ prototype }
;
;	STD	implemented; the function is "sys_NAME", and SYS_NAME is its
;		number (syscall.h).
;	The numbers are V86BSD's own, not Linux's (the Linux numbers are in
;	compat/linux/syscalls.master).  The first six are OpenBSD's.  A number
;	is never reused or renumbered: a new call goes at the end.  A number
;	that is not listed is not implemented (sys_nosys: ENOSYS).
;	The arguments are the same as Linux's for now (struct layouts too).
;
;	Written by makesyscalls.sh into sys/syscall.h, sys/syscallargs.h and
;	kern/init_sysent.c (sh kern/makesyscalls.sh kern/syscalls.conf).

1	STD	{ long sys_exit(long code); }
2	STD	{ long sys_fork(void); }
